WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-, Golden Globe-,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.838
and Academy Award-winning
actress you know from films

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
such as "Still Alice,"
"Far From Heaven,"

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.009 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and "Crazy Stupid Love."

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's currently starring
in "Bel Canto,"

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is in select theaters
this Friday

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
and will be available
on digital and On Demand.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.385 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:21.721 line:92%
-[ Singing in foreign language ]

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:38.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the show
Julianne Moore.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.343 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:59.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Welcome.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.362 line:92%
-Thank you for having me.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.797 line:92%
-I am thrilled to have you here.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is
one of my favorite books.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love "Bel Canto."
It's a beautiful book.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.001 line:92%
-A beautiful, beautiful book.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're playing --
anyone could have guessed --

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
an opera singer.
-I am, of course.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.673
Yes, that's right.
-Of everything you've taken on,

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
that must have been
a very difficult task.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, it's so hard.
I can't sing.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was
Renée Fleming's voice.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That wasn't mine.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
in order to do that,

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to try
to learn to sing,

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.623
so I studied with her coach,
and I watched a lot of opera,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I went to The Met,
and I did all this

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
other stuff
to learn about opera.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I was --
Because in that scene,

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
it really pushes in on you,

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.734
and when I was watching it,
I was like, "Oh, you have to --"

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't just open your mouth
and move it.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to make
your whole body --

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-It's not just lip-sync video.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that was particularly bad
because it was outside.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would ask them to crank
it up as loud as possible

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.114 line:92%
so that people wouldn't hear me.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
But because it was outside,
we couldn't control the sound.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.887
-So you were --
Were you singing at full volume?

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:01.754 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I guess you have to.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was pretty
humiliating.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.891 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was there ever a situation
where people would say,

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.196 size:78% position:39%
"Hey, you know what?
You're not that bad."

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Paul Weitz, the director,
would say that to me.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think he's --
-He's very nice.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know Paul.
He's very nice.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really nice guy.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.573
But you realize everybody in the
sound department can hear you

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.209
because you're mic'd, so they're
the ones who are there,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.811 line:92%
holding the boom, going...

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, for those
who don't know the book,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's this really, uh,
sort of a --

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wouldn't guess
from the title

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact
that you're an opera --

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's this thrilling story
about this hostage situation.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.393 line:92%
-It's based on a true story,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:44.664
the 1996 hostage situation
in Peru at the Japanese embassy.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
There wasn't
an opera singer there,

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that's invented,
but it really is --

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a political thriller
and a love story.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And one of the other
wonderful things,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of
the actual real story,

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's also this wonderful
multiethnic cast.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.712
Because it was all these people
trapped in an embassy who --

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.613 size:75% position:38% line:92%
You know, there's --

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
translator plays a huge role

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
because people
can't communicate.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.652 size:75% position:38%
-And everybody spoke
their own language,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
so there's Japanese
and English and Spanish

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
and French
and German and Polish.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:11.891 line:92%
And there was an actress --

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually,
a Guatemalan actress --

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.394 line:92%
who just learned Spanish.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she still
spoke Guatemalan sometimes,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was
an indigenous language.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was amazing.
And nothing --

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:24.070
you know, and Ken Watanabe
plays my, I guess, boyfriend?

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'm gonna
sign off on boyfriend.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he only
speaks Japanese to me,

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.344 line:92%
and I only speak English to him.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there are times
when we just don't --

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.048 line:92%
we just communicate, you know,

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
in, like,
boyfriend/girlfriend language.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:41.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it was what made it
such a beautiful book.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.923 line:92%
And, yes, a romantic thriller,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
well-executed both on the page
and in the film,

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is really nice.
-Nice.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:50.997
-You are -- just finished a film
in Upstate New York with your --

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:51.864 line:92%
that your husband directed?

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Long Island.
Oyster bay, actually.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.168 line:92%
In Manhattan and in India.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were -- and, yeah.
All those places.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:57.737 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And you had visitors --

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.573
When you're working on a movie
set, sometimes visitors stop by.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
They want to see
the magic of a film set.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.309 line:92%
-Well, yeah, and, you know,

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oyster Bay may not
seem like the country.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:09.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it is deep, deep country,
with lots and lots of,

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
different kinds of wildlife.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.686
-And this was --
This is an actual video you took

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the --
This would be craft service?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is late at night
at catering,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
after things
are being cleared up.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's see the help you got
on the cleanup.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:28.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.969 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-There they are, yeah.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:30.937 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:33.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you go --
They dip in afterward.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.841 line:92%
You see them going, like...

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wait a minute, wait a minute,
one more thing down there."

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.679 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah. They're like,
"Look, we understand

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:40.413 size:78% position:39% line:92%
this is a closed set.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
We will be out of here
in a second."

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're both gonna grab
one more --

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna grab
two more things.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
That's right, yeah.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.689
-You have had some interactions
with the wildlife recently.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.490 line:92%
This was not your only one.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we had a really, really
exciting thing happen.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:54.994 line:92%
I mean, not just the raccoons,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:57.997
but we had a turtle birth
in our pool this summer.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so, now,
is that something

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.601 size:81% position:41%
you only find out once
the turtles are there?

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.304
-Okay, so you don't see a
pregnant turtle walking around.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
Nothing like that.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they just --
they literally appear.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what happens is,
turtles crawl up,

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:13.313
they crawl into your yard and
they lay their eggs somewhere.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
when the babies are hatched,

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
they crawl toward
the nearest water source,

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they think
that's their environment,

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it just happened
to be our pool.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, it's interesting
because if you'd have told me

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
how many turtles
are born at once...

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wouldn't know, yeah.
-I wouldn't know.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was over what I thought.
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:31.898
-That's a lot of turtles, right?
-That's a lot of turtles.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But that's nothing like,
you know,

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
delivering your own child
in a lobby.

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.770
-Right.
-So I'm saying this turtle birth

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
is nothing
to what you experienced.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, that's right.
My wife had a baby in a lobby.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think, like,
I would just say that

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.546
that mom turtle did nothing
compared to what she did.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, nothing compared
to what she did.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, that's beautiful grass.
-Yes, exactly.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.152
-Yeah.
We were nowhere near your pool.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
If she'd only had
a water source.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right, you wouldn't
have been in the lobby.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.426
-As she was like --
She's like, "The baby's coming.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get me
to Julianne Moore's pool."

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "We're too far away.
We're too far away."

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:07.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not gonna make it.
-"I don't know where it is!"

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:10.370
Uh, this is very exciting to me,
as well.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause, obviously,
our kids are young.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
They cannot be involved
in our professional life yet,

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
but your daughter
worked on set for the film.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:20.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she did.
She was a P.A.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.314 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and an official --

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:23.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was very nice to see
that you did not --

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was not some situation
where she was elevated

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
due to the fact
that her father was directing

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.523
and her mother was in the film.
-No, she's gonna work, man.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She was working.
-She's gonna work.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.559
-This is her job right there.
That is real work, right there.

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:35.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what she's gonna do.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:38.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fully...
Fully holding an umbrella.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I was hot.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.569
-I was super, super hot,
so somebody's gonna do it.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And I would imagine that would

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.807
literally be the only way
you could get your daughter

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
to hold an umbrella over you.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:52.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is to hire her.
-She's 16.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:53.546 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She's not gonna do that.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:56.048
But, you know, she had
a headset and stuff, too,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so she took her job
very seriously.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
She'd be like, "Yeah,
no, I have eyes on Julie.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, she's right here."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I got her. No.
Oh, no, no, no. She's 10-1,"

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
which means that
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:07.460
I'm like, "You don't have
to tell them everything!"

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.963 size:81% position:41%
She's like, "No, I do.
That's my job, Mom."

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:11.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's so lovely
that it's a family affair.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
